access.revoked | async | committed | ws-access-recheck | replicated: recheck.ws-access
access.revoked | async | committed | sse-access-revoked | replicated: recheck.sse-revocation
account.erased | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | provider-model-cache | replicated: providers.model-listings
account.erased | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | knowledge-embedder-cache | replicated: rag.embedders
account.erased | async | committed | ws-access-recheck | replicated: recheck.ws-access
credential.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | provider-model-cache | replicated: providers.model-listings
credential.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | knowledge-embedder-cache | replicated: rag.embedders
finding.assigned | async | committed | finding-assignment-fanout | local: sends an email and writes a bell row: a side effect that must happen once
finding.commented | async | committed | finding-comment-fanout | local: sends an email and writes bell rows: a side effect that must happen once, and the comment text stays on this replica
flow.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | dashboard-cache | replicated: dashboard.analytics, dashboard.home
flow.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | chat-context-cache | local: keys carry the flow version, so another replica misses on a new version; the drop is hygiene
flow.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | flow-search-index | local: served only for the exact document object it was built from, which each replica resolves through its own version-checked read
flow.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | flow-document-cache | local: every read re-checks the stored version, so another replica's change or delete is seen at once
flow.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | analyzer-report-cache | local: a report is a function of the document, rule profile and analyzer version; another replica recomputes on a miss
flow.changed | async | committed | ws-flow-changed | local: the hub broadcasts through the WebSocket room backplane, which already reaches every replica's viewers when Redis is configured
flow.changed | async | committed | ws-access-recheck | replicated: recheck.ws-access
knowledge_doc.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | knowledge-corpus-count | replicated: rag.corpus-counts
org_member.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | rule-profiles | replicated: rules.profiles
org_member.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | provider-model-cache | replicated: providers.model-listings
org_member.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | knowledge-corpus-count | replicated: rag.corpus-counts
org_member.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | knowledge-embedder-cache | replicated: rag.embedders
org_member.changed | async | committed | lent-credential-revocation | local: a keystore write with audit rows: it must happen once, and the shared keystore makes it visible to every replica
org_member.changed | async | committed | ws-access-recheck | replicated: recheck.ws-access
settings.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | settings-cache | replicated: settings.deployment
settings.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | rule-profiles | replicated: rules.deployment-profile, rules.profiles
settings.changed | sync | immediate+committed+rolled-back | knowledge-embedder-cache | replicated: rag.embedders
